  "notes": "Module whose defaults create only the VPC, random_integer, random_shuffle and AZ data source; subnets, route tables, IGW and endpoints are count/for_each gated and are checked as declared capabilities. Not checked: the configurable maximum subnet count (the adapter resolves the shuffle result_count to the variable default, so a variable and a literal look alike) and the name-prefix variable names (prompt does not name them). The private route table is the gated declared table with no route block; the public one is the table whose route names an internet gateway (a separate aws_route to the IGW is not linked to its table, a rare form). private_assoc shows the private table has associations; that all three tiers are associated cannot be counted, since one for_each association over all private subnets is also valid."
